{"agent":"impact","findings":[{"id":"impact-1","file":"src/python/model/model.py","line":81,"title":"sanitize_log_value runs on every add/remove/update call even when DEBUG logging is off","category":"perf-at-scale","cwe":null,"severity":"low","agent_confidence":30,"in_diff":true,"intent_doc_match":null,"problem":"The debug message is built with eager str.format(), so sanitize_log_value runs before the logger checks whether DEBUG is enabled. sanitize_log_value (src/python/common/types.py:45-58) does two str.replace passes and then a Python-level loop over every character, appending each one to a list. model_builder.py:129 calls Model.add_file for every file on every model rebuild, and controller.py:587-591 calls add/remove/update for every diff entry. The cost is O(total filename chars) per scan, paid even in production where DEBUG is usually off. The old code already paid the eager .format cost. The new cost is only the per-character loop, which is small for filenames. pending: measure scan-cycle time with a large file tree (tens of thousands of entries) to confirm the cost matters.","current_code":"self.logger.debug(\"LftpModel: Adding file '{}'\".format(sanitize_log_value(file.name)))","fix_hint":"Optionally use lazy logging args (logger.debug(\"... '%s'\", sanitize_log_value(...)) still runs eagerly), so guard with self.logger.isEnabledFor(logging.DEBUG) if profiling shows it matters.","why_it_matters":"Negligible at normal scale. It only matters if very large remote trees make model rebuilds hot.","silenced_marker_nearby":false}],"agent_notes":["The change tightens a control: three debug log calls in Model.add_file, remove_file and update_file now pass their values through the existing sanitize_log_value helper (CWE-117). It changes only what text reaches the log. Model behaviour, return values and exceptions are unchanged.","No public API change: the signatures of add_file, remove_file and update_file are unchanged. The only new import is sanitize_log_value, which common/__init__.py:1 re-exports, so the import cannot fail.","Type safety: sanitize_log_value calls value.replace and needs a str. ModelFile.name is typed str and is set in the constructor (model/file.py:34-35, 128). The only production caller of remove_file passes diff.old_file.name (controller.py:589), which is also a str. No path passes None or a non-str, so this adds no new crash risk before the ModelError checks.","Blast radius: Model is imported by 13 modules (controller, auto_queue, extract dispatch/process, file_operation_manager, model_builder, diff, web stream_model, serialize, web_app_builder). Only these three log lines change, so a bug here would at worst throw from inside add/remove/update. Given the str invariant, that is very unlikely.","Behaviour change for log readers: filenames with control characters (TAB, ESC, CR/LF, DEL) now appear as \\xHH, \\r or \\n escapes in debug logs. Any log-scraping tooling that grepped for raw filenames with such characters would no longer match. This is the intended effect.","Pre-existing gap, not introduced here: by design, sanitize_log_value leaves C1 controls (0x80-0x9F) and Unicode bidi or line-separator characters (U+2028, U+202E) unescaped. That gap applies to every existing caller of the helper and is out of scope for this diff.","No database, schema or migration changes.","Verdict: shippable as-is. The only finding is a low-confidence perf note."]}
